    <bpmn:process id="W_W1289" name="W1289. Store-Level Tool Demonstration &amp; Product Launch Event Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor requests in-store product demonstration; or Category Manager schedules product launch event
Frequency: ~2–4 vendor demos per store per month; ~1 major product launch per quarter per store
Volume: ~400–800 vendor demos chain-wide per month; ~200 product launch events per quarter
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Department Supervisor, Sales Associate, Vendor Representative, Store Manager, Marketing
Source: workflow W1289 — Store-Level Tool Demonstration &amp; Product Launch Event Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1289_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1289_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1289_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1289_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1289_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1289_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1289_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1289_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1289_Lane2" name="Vendor Representative">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1289_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1289_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1289_Start4" name="Vendor requests in-store product demonstration; or Category Manager schedules product…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1289_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1289_Task5" name="Event scheduling &amp; vendor coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Event scheduling &amp; vendor coordination: Department Supervisor coordinates with vendor representative: (a) confirm demo date (preferably weekend for maximum foot traffic), (b) identify featured products and demo format (hands-on trial, comparison, expert demonstration), (c) confirm vendor will provide: demonstration units, marketing materials (banners, flyers), product specialist/brand ambassador, and any special pricing for event period, (d) for major launches: coordinate with Marketing for advertising support per W676 and social media promotion per PA-14.2
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Vendor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1289_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1289_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1289_Task6" name="Store preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store preparation: Department Supervisor prepares demo area: (a) designate space (preferably near featured product aisle or at store entrance for high visibility), (b) set up demonstration table with power outlets, extension cords, safety barriers, (c) ensure adequate inventory of featured products on shelves (coordinate with replenishment per W4), (d) prepare promotional price tags and special event signage, (e) brief Sales Associates on featured products, special pricing, and sales talking points
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1289_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1289_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1289_Task7" name="Event execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Event execution: Vendor representative conducts product demonstration: (a) present product features and benefits, (b) allow customers hands-on trial with supervision, (c) Sales Associates assist with product questions and facilitate purchase, (d) collect customer contact details (loyalty sign-ups, lead capture for follow-up), (e) Department Supervisor monitors crowd flow and safety compliance per VS-24 HSE (power tools, electrical safety), (f) for power tools: ensure dust collection, hearing protection available, and safety guards in place
Responsible (R): Vendor Representative / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1289_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1289_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1289_Task8" name="Sales tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Sales tracking: During and after event: (a) system tracks featured product sales vs. baseline (same day previous week), (b) track customer engagement (demo participants, leads captured, loyalty sign-ups), (c) Sales Associates log customer feedback and product reactions, (d) end-of-day: Department Supervisor reviews event sales performance
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1289_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1289_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1289_Task9" name="Post-event reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-event reconciliation: (a) Department Supervisor reconciles vendor-provided demo units (return, retain as display, or purchase per vendor agreement), (b) remove event-specific promotional pricing and signage, (c) restore demo area to normal merchandising layout, (d) unsold event inventory returned to stock or flagged for return per W1280
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1289_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1289_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1289_Task10" name="Event performance report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Event performance report: Department Supervisor submits event report to Category Manager: (a) sales lift (featured product sales vs. baseline), (b) customer engagement metrics, (c) customer feedback summary, (d) inventory sold vs. provided, (e) vendor representative performance, (f) recommendations for future events; Category Manager aggregates chain-wide event data for vendor negotiation per W688
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1289_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1289_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1289_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1289_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-277 (ensure controlled execution — Workshops &amp; Events (PA-12.3).) | - operational: safety briefing, protective equipment, and supervision required per W440
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1289_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1289_Annotation12" targetRef="W1289_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1289_Flow14" sourceRef="W1289_Start4" targetRef="W1289_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1289_Flow15" sourceRef="W1289_Task5" targetRef="W1289_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1289_Flow16" sourceRef="W1289_Task6" targetRef="W1289_Task7" />
