    <bpmn:process id="W_W1556" name="W1556. Youth &amp; Student Skilled Trade Exposure Program, TESDA Partnership &amp; School Career Day Participation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual community engagement calendar; or TESDA partnership cycle; or school invitation for career day; or BuildRight workforce pipeline need (recruitment per W172)
Frequency: ~2–4 school/career events per store per year; ~400–800 events/year chain-wide; TESDA partnership activities quarterly
Volume: 200 stores × ~3 events/year; each event reaches 50–200 students; ~30,000–120,000 student touchpoints/year (600 events × 50–200)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Department Supervisor, HR Training Manager, TESDA Representative, School Administrator, Sales Associates
Source: workflow W1556 — Youth &amp; Student Skilled Trade Exposure Program, TESDA Partnership &amp; School Career Day Participation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1556_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1556_Lane1" name="HR Training Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1556_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1556_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1556_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1556_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1556_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1556_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1556_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1556_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1556_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1556_Start5" name="Annual community engagement calendar; or TESDA partnership cycle; or school invitation…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1556_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1556_Task6" name="TESDA partnership establishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: TESDA partnership establishment: HR Training Manager establishes formal partnership with regional TESDA offices: (a) sign Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) allowing BuildRight stores to serve as practical training venues for TESDA scholar trainees; (b) agree on training modules: basic electrical wiring, plumbing installation, tile setting, carpentry, paint application; (c) BuildRight provides: venue (store workshop area per W147), materials (sample tiles, pipes, wires, lumber from damaged/returns stock), and Department Supervisors as resource persons; (d) TESDA provides: curriculum, certification assessment, and scholar recruitment; (e) target: 2–3 TESDA partnerships per region (Mindanao, Visayas, Luzon, NCR)
Responsible (R): HR Training Manager / CHRO
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 20 hours (one-time setup)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1556_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1556_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1556_Task7" name="School career day participation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: School career day participation: Store Manager or Department Supervisor represents BuildRight at local high school and vocational school career days: (a) set up BuildRight booth with: tool displays (hand tools and power tools), construction material samples, trade career information flyers, BuildRight employment opportunities; (b) interactive demo: basic woodworking or electrical wiring demonstration for students; (c) promote construction trades as viable career: earning potential (skilled electrician: PHP 25–40K/month; master plumber: PHP 30–50K/month in Metro Manila), TESDA certification pathway, BuildRight trade account benefits for future contractors; (d) distribute BuildRight scholarship information for TESDA programs (if BuildRight sponsors scholars)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 4–6 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1556_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1556_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1556_Task8" name="In-store youth workshop series">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: In-store youth workshop series: Quarterly, select stores host &quot;BuildRight Future Builders&quot; workshops for youth (ages 16–25): (a) 4-hour Saturday workshop covering: (i) basic tool safety (hand tools, portable power tools), (ii) hands-on project: build a simple shelf, install a light fixture, or lay tile on a sample board, (iii) career paths in construction and home improvement; (b) Department Supervisors serve as instructors; materials sourced from returns/damaged stock per W1513; (c) each workshop limited to 15–20 participants; pre-registration per W147 workshop registration system; (d) participants receive BuildRight certificate of completion and discount coupon for tool purchases
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / HR Training Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 6 hours/workshop</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1556_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1556_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1556_Task9" name="Youth internship pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Youth internship pipeline: BuildRight offers a structured internship program for TESDA scholars and vocational students: (a) 2–4 week internship at a BuildRight store in: (i) store operations (receiving, stocking, customer service), (ii) department-specific (paint mixing, lumber yard, tool rental), (iii) basic trade exposure (shadowing trade counter interactions); (b) Store Manager assigns intern to a Department Supervisor as mentor; (c) intern receives daily allowance (PHP 300–500/day) and BuildRight work experience certificate; (d) at internship completion: evaluate intern for potential full-time employment per W172 recruitment pipeline; (e) target: ~1 intern/store/year across the chain ≈ 200 interns/year ≈ ~400 internship-management hours/year (per the Time Estimate)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HR Training Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2 hours/intern</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1556_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1556_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1556_Task10" name="Annual program effectiveness review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual program effectiveness review: HR Training Manager reviews youth program outcomes: (a) number of events conducted, students reached, workshops delivered; (b) conversion metrics: (i) % of workshop attendees who later open trade accounts at BuildRight, (ii) % of interns hired as full-time employees, (iii) TESDA partnership satisfaction survey; (c) cost vs. benefit: program cost (materials, staff time, venue, allowances) vs. lifetime value of converted customers and employees; (d) adjust program scope and focus for next year based on results
Responsible (R): HR Training Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1556_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1556_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1556_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1556_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-277 (ensure controlled execution — Workshops &amp; Events (PA-12.3).) | - operational: tracking program participants in CRM for future outreach
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1556_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1556_Annotation12" targetRef="W1556_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
