    <bpmn:process id="W_W1557" name="W1557. Seasonal DIY Workshop Series Planning, Content Development &amp; Customer Conversion Funnel Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly workshop calendar planning; or seasonal merchandise focus shift (per seasonal calendar in model company profile Section 13.2); or vendor co-marketing opportunity
Frequency: Quarterly planning cycle; ~6–9 workshop sessions per store per quarter (2–3/month per W1378); ~1,200–1,800 workshops/quarter chain-wide
Volume: 200 stores × 6–9 sessions/quarter × 4 quarters = ~4,800–7,200 workshops/year; ~10–20 participants per workshop
Owner: Marketing Manager (Content)
Participants: Marketing Manager, Category Manager, Store Manager, Department Supervisor (instructor), Content Creator, Ecommerce Manager
Source: workflow W1557 — Seasonal DIY Workshop Series Planning, Content Development &amp; Customer Conversion Funnel Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1557_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1557_Lane1" name="Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1557_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1557_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1557_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1557_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1557_Lane2" name="Content Creator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1557_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1557_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1557_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1557_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1557_Start5" name="Quarterly workshop calendar planning; or seasonal merchandise focus shift (per seasonal…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1557_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1557_Task6" name="Quarterly topic selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly topic selection: Marketing Manager and Category Managers jointly select 2–3 workshop topics per quarter aligned with seasonal merchandise focus: (a) Q1 (Jan–Mar): &quot;Refresh Your Home&quot; series — (i) Interior Paint Color Selection &amp; Application Techniques, (ii) DIY Tile Backsplash Installation, (iii) Basic Electrical: Install a Ceiling Fan; (b) Q2 (Apr–Jun): &quot;Summer Ready&quot; series — (i) Garden &amp; Outdoor Living Setup, (ii) Aircon Selection &amp; Basic Maintenance, (iii) Waterproofing Your Roof Before the Rains; (c) Q3 (Jul–Sep): &quot;Rainy Season Solutions&quot; series — (i) Waterproofing &amp; Leak Repair, (ii) Emergency Plumbing: Fixing Common Leaks, (iii) Home Security: Install Outdoor Lighting &amp; Locks; (d) Q4 (Oct–Dec): &quot;Holiday Home&quot; series — (i) Holiday Lighting &amp; Electrical Safety, (ii) DIY Shelving &amp; Storage Solutions, (iii) Gift-Worthy Weekend Projects
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager / Category Managers
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1557_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1557_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1557_Task7" name="Content development">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Content development: Marketing team develops workshop content for each topic: (a) Content Creator produces: (i) instructor guide (step-by-step lesson plan for Department Supervisor), (ii) participant handout (project overview, materials list with SKU numbers, step-by-step instructions with photos), (iii) promotional materials (social media graphics, in-store posters, email template per W1350); (b) Category Manager ensures materials list features BuildRight products: (i) all materials available in-store (no items that are special-order only), (ii) bundle pricing for workshop participants (e.g., &quot;Workshop Attendee Kit: everything you need for PHP 2,500 — save 15%&quot;), (iii) featured products aligned with current promotions per W13
Responsible (R): Content Creator / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Marketing Manager
Duration: 8–12 hours/topic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1557_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1557_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1557_Task8" name="Registration &amp; promotion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Registration &amp; promotion: (a) workshops listed on buildright.com.ph and mobile app with online registration per W147; (b) Marketing sends targeted email invitations: (i) loyalty members who purchased related category items in the past 6 months (e.g., paint workshop invite to customers who bought paint supplies), (ii) trade account customers for advanced topics, (iii) new loyalty members (welcome series includes workshop calendar); (c) in-store promotion: Department Supervisors mention upcoming workshops to interested customers during floor interactions; (d) social media promotion per W142: &quot;DIY Saturday at BuildRight [store name] — learn to [topic] this weekend! Limited slots, register now&quot;; (e) target: 10–20 registrations per workshop
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager / Ecommerce Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–3 hours/workshop</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1557_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1557_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1557_Task9" name="Workshop delivery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Workshop delivery: Department Supervisor delivers workshop per instructor guide (W147 operational execution); additional conversion-focused elements: (a) materials kit available for purchase at the end of the workshop at discounted bundle price; (b) loyalty points bonus: attendees earn 2x points on purchases made within 7 days of the workshop; (c) Department Supervisor demonstrates using specific BuildRight SKUs (not generic tools) — participants see exactly what to buy
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/workshop</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1557_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1557_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1557_Task10" name="Conversion funnel tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Conversion funnel tracking: Marketing Manager tracks the workshop-to-purchase conversion funnel: (a) registrations → attendance rate (target: &gt; 70%); (b) attendance → post-workshop purchase rate within 7 days (target: &gt; 40%); (c) post-workshop average transaction value vs. non-attendee ATV (target: +25%); (d) category penetration: workshop attendees purchasing in the featured category (paint workshop → paint department sales); (e) quarterly: compile conversion funnel data and adjust topics, content, and promotion strategy based on what drives highest conversion
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager / Data Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1557_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1557_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1557_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1557_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-277 (ensure controlled execution — Workshops &amp; Events (PA-12.3).) | - operational: train-the-trainer sessions during quarterly meetings and video examples of best-practice delivery
Owner: Marketing Manager (Content)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
